          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This means that the line cuts the y-axis at a distance of 2 units from the origin in the negative direction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.146,
            0.884,
            0.186
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After observing the graphs in Figures 2.8 to 2.14, we may conclude the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.193,
            0.884,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) In the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = a x + b ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , a represents the slope of the line and b represents the y-intercept."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.24,
            0.884,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) If we change the values of a, keeping b fixed, the slope of the line changes while the y-intercept remains fixed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.287,
            0.886,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) If we change the values of b keeping the value of a fixed, the lines shift but remain parallel to the original line. Thus, lines with equal slopes but different y-intercepts are parallel to each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.374,
            0.404,
            0.622,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 2.6"
